// Rule: [T1204] Operation Dream Job - Securitypdf Temp Child Execution
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1204
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Campaign hunt for a trojanized PDF viewer creating and launching a decrypted executable from the Windows temporary directory.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for securitypdf temp child execution using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: The endpoint recorded the exact campaign parent- child execution pattern and requires immediate file collection and lineage review.
// A match does not prove: Malicious PDF content, successful Troy loading, zero- day exploitation, SYSTEM privilege, EDR impairment, C2 or Lazarus attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Operation Dream Job / SecurityPDF child execution
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint process creation events
// Source evidence: Check Point Research observed SecurityPDF.exe writing and
// launching %TEMP%\new.exe after a crafted PDF was opened.
// No threshold, rarity, join, sequence, hash, domain, or attribution is used.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "SecurityPDF.exe"
| where FileName =~ "new.exe"
| where FolderPath contains @"\Temp\"
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    AccountDomain,
    AccountName,
    AccountUpn,
    FileName,
    FolderPath,
    ProcessCommandLine,
    ProcessId,
    ProcessUniqueId,
    ProcessIntegrityLevel,
    ProcessTokenElevation,
    SHA1,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessId,
    InitiatingProcessUniqueId,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessAccountUpn,
    IsProcessRemoteSession,
    ProcessRemoteSessionIP,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
